-- title:
--   Completions away from q are integrally closed domains
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, and a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, with finite residue field, in which $\ell_g$ and $M'$ are units. Assume: the compatibility hypotheses `hℓ`, `hM`, `hL` asserting that the $\Gamma_1$-point condition (a point $(x_P,y_P)$ on the affine curve with $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell_g}(x_P)=0$ and $(x_Q,y_Q)=(x_P,y_P)$), the $\Gamma_0(p^k)$ cyclic-kernel-generator condition, and the divisibility of `inLineMulPoly` are preserved under Weierstrass variable changes; a family $\mathcal{G}$ of relative group laws on the projective models, which is chord-tangent and has the origin as identity section; a transport $\mathcal{T}$ of Drinfeld pairs of level $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport`; and the hypotheses `hVC`, `hCO` providing graded ring homomorphisms realising variable changes and coefficient maps on the projective-model gradings. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the moduli datum attached to `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓg M' q …`, that is, an $A_0$-algebra $B_0$ with a universal point representing that datum, and assume $B_0$ is of finite type over $A_0$. Then for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of $B_0$ not containing the image of $q$, the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $B_0$ is a domain, is integrally closed, and the image of $q$ in it is nonzero.
--
--   This is the local normality statement for the fine moduli ring of the $H_1$-type level structure at the points of characteristic zero, i.e. those lying over the generic point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_0$. It feeds the analysis of the minimal primes of $B_0$ and of flatness and integral closedness of the corresponding quotients.
